# Auroral Procession: "Return target card from your graveyard to your hand." Bot2's drawn Lightning Bolt is discarded at the
# end of turn 2, so on turn 3 Bot1's own graveyard holds only the Black Lotus it sacrifices for mana. A cast naming Bot2's
# Bolt is refused (the card is in the wrong graveyard), so is one naming the Mox Emerald on the battlefield (not in a
# graveyard at all), and the cast at the Lotus is the positive control: the Lotus is back in Bot1's hand and the Bolt stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Auroral Procession
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Island x3
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Auroral Procession.Cast(Bot2.Graveyard.Lightning Bolt)
! Bot1.Hand.Auroral Procession.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald)
Bot1.Hand.Auroral Procession.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Black Lotus)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Auroral Procession
Bot1.Hand = Black Lotus; Island; Island; Island; Island
